# ─── Kotoba frontend (.env.local) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` at the project root (NOT inside app/).
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are exposed to the browser bundle; KOTOBA_WEB_PASSWORD (below) is server-side only.

# Backend URL — ONE knob, two modes:
#   unset/empty (local default) → SAME-ORIGIN PROXY mode: the browser talks only to this app's own
#     origin and Next rewrites /api/* to the backend server-side. No CORS, no cross-site cookies,
#     one URL — a fresh clone just works. The voice WebSocket still dials the backend directly
#     (WebSockets don't survive Next rewrites); its address comes from KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL below.
#   set → DIRECT mode: the browser calls this URL itself. Use it when frontend and backend live on
#     different public origins (e.g. Vercel frontend + tunnel/Railway backend). Docker compose uses
#     the proxy mode: both containers share a network, so leaving this unset is correct there.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-backend.example.com

# Proxy-mode only: where the Next server (and the voice WebSocket) reach the backend.
# Ignored when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is set.
# KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# PROXY mode only, and only when the BROWSER cannot reach KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL: the ws:// or wss://
# origin the voice socket dials, since WebSockets don't survive the rewrite. Unset, it is derived from
# KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL — right on a laptop, wrong under docker compose, where `backend:8000` resolves
# only inside the compose network (that image passes the published host port instead). Ignored in
# DIRECT mode, where the socket already carries NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL's own origin, and in the packaged
# build, where it dials the page's origin because the backend is what served the page.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VOICE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000

# ElevenLabs Conversational-AI agent ID. Needed ONLY by the "agent" voice transport below, which is
# not the default: local voice speaks and listens with no agent at all. Also settable in Settings.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# Voice transport: "local" (default — browser ↔ backend WebSocket, no tunnel needed) or "agent"
# (ElevenLabs Conversational-AI agent; EL's cloud must reach the backend, so it needs a public URL).
# Also settable live from the Settings panel (runtime voice_mode, which wins over this).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KOTOBA_VOICE_MODE=local

# LEGACY, and kept working on purpose. Which Live2D model she wears is chosen at RUNTIME now: the
# backend serves models from ~/.kotoba/models (KOTOBA_MODELS_DIR) and the app asks it at startup, so
# there is nothing to set here and nothing to rebuild. These two still name a model in public/models/
# for anyone who set them up before that, and are used ONLY while ~/.kotoba/models is empty — install
# a model there and it takes over. Next inlines them at build time, which is why they stopped being
# the control.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE2D_MODEL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE2D_ENTRY=

# Framing, for a model shaped differently from the default: canvas height over the model's native
# height, and her centre as a fraction of canvas height (above 1 pushes the body off-screen so only
# the face shows). These apply to whichever model was chosen. Unset → the profile's own numbers.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE2D_SCALE=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVE2D_ANCHOR_Y=

# Optional: gate password. When set, the app asks for this password on first load
# and sends it to the backend as a Bearer token or ?token= param for all /api/* calls.
# Leave unset for local dev (no gate — the backend's /api gate is open too, everything just works).
# To enable the gate, set KOTOBA_WEB_PASSWORD to the SAME value here and in api/.env — one secret,
# one name, both sides. (KOTOBA_GATE_PASSWORD is a legacy alias, accepted here and by the backend but
# used only when KOTOBA_WEB_PASSWORD is unset — the canonical name always wins if both are set. Both
# sides resolve in that same order, so a deployment that still sets only the legacy name keeps working.)
# KOTOBA_WEB_PASSWORD=

# Optional: key used to HMAC-sign the gate's session cookie. Leave it unset — the gate password above
# is used as the signing key. Set it only to rotate every logged-in session without changing the
# password (or the reverse). It is NOT a password: on its own it does not enable the gate.
# KOTOBA_GATE_SECRET=
